From: Jeremy Melanson <1080872+zish@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:16:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: seal the spike's history, bookmarks, logins and cards

The spike's Fenix gives places', the logins' and autofill's stores a
key each, an HMAC of the browser's own key in the vault under a label
of its own, which waits for the vault's key: none of the three
databases is opened before the vault is open to the browser
(encri-firefox, stage 3; docs/sealed-history.md).

The gate gains stage 3's controls: --es sealing on|off for the control
run, --es seal write|read|forget|plain with a marker, and --ei
placesbench, which times places in the clear and sealed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
